      }
    }
  ],
  "keyInsight": "A chemical bond forms exactly at the distance where the system reaches its lowest potential energy, balancing the attraction of electrons to nuclei with the repulsion between the nuclei.",
  "reconstructionNotes": "The curve is a classic Morse potential shape. The slider controls a locator point on the curve AND the physical distance between a pair of dynamic green spheres rendered in the graph area. The static annotations ('too close', 'bond length', 'too far') and their corresponding static sphere graphics should sit transparently in the background, becoming fully opaque/highlighted when the slider's dynamic point (or a direct click) enters their respective regions (x < 60, 60 < x < 100, x > 100)."
}

